From be16546be24117fa31a5d0891218b11cb6912df3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Leech <andrew.leech@planetinnovation.com.au>
Date: Fri, 27 Mar 2026 07:15:59 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] extmod/btstack: Implement pairing and bonding support.

Adds BLE pairing/bonding for BTstack by implementing TLV-backed key
storage that delegates to Python's IRQ_GET_SECRET/IRQ_SET_SECRET
handlers, enabling bond persistence across sessions. Switches the
device database from le_device_db_memory to le_device_db_tlv, adds
encryption state caching to deduplicate events, handles SM events
(Just Works, passkey display/input, numeric comparison), and
implements gap_passkey(). Trims unused BTstack sources from the cmake
build. Adds port-specific ER/IR key generation using hardware RNG on
rp2/stm32 and /dev/urandom on unix. Enables pairing/bonding config
flag on rp2.

Signed-off-by: Andrew Leech <andrew.leech@planetinnovation.com.au>
